cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Mimic in your research, please cite it as below, together with the papers of the model package you use (each package's README lists them)."
title: "Mimic"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Croton
    given-names: Darren
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5009-512X"
abstract: "Mimic is a physics-agnostic galaxy evolution framework. Its core owns merger-tree processing, memory, input and output, validation and output provenance; the physics lives in model packages of runtime modules, and each merger-tree catalogue in a simulation package."
repository-code: "https://github.com/darrencroton/mimic"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - galaxy formation
  - galaxy evolution
  - semi-analytic model
  - merger trees
